=== ev-testimony
talks: coalition, kawaguchi, sen-x=talk-sen
actions: rally, push

--- start
Hearing day. Forty testifiers are signed up — teachers, a school cook, two ranchers, a hotel housekeeper with her whole shift outside. Two minutes each. The chair is already checking his watch. Somebody has to go first.
MOBILIZING: The cook feeds four hundred kids a day. Put the number in the room, not just the argument.
TALK STORY: The ranchers flip a room faster than anyone expects — 'small business supports this' still moves skeptics.

* The school cook goes first.
  {+4 support}
  Two minutes, no notes. The chair stops checking his watch. Twitter does the rest.

* The ranchers go first.
  {+3 influence, +1 support}
  'We're not anti-business — we ARE the business.' Two committee skeptics visibly recalibrate.

* [MOBILIZING 12 white] Neither. Fill the room past the sign-up sheet and let him try to gavel it.
  mods: support/30
  _ante: The ante (engine: a checked choice's own `effects` are paid on commit, win or lose). Packing a room past the sign-up sheet SPENDS the base — you are asking people to take an unpaid morning off before you know whether the chair will seat them. It is printed on the button with the odds.
  {-3 support}
  pass:
    {+7 support, -1 influence}
    By 9:40 the overflow room is full and they open a second overflow room. The chair, on the record, extends testimony by ninety minutes. Nobody in that hallway forgets that they are the reason.
  fail:
    {-3 support}
    Twenty-two show. The overflow room stays dark and the chair caps testimony at forty minutes, politely. The housekeeper who took an unpaid morning off does not get called.
